  ======================================================================
  DEPTH DECOMPOSITION
  ======================================================================

  D(n) = D1(n) + D2(n) + D3(n) + ...
  where Dd(n) = sum over odd partitions with d parts > 1

    n           D1           D2           D3      D_total     D_actual
    3       2.0000       0.0000       0.0000       2.0000       2.0000
    4       4.0000       0.0000       0.0000       4.0000       4.0000
    5      12.0000       0.0000       0.0000      12.0000      12.0000
    6      29.3333      10.6667       0.0000      40.0000      40.0000
    7     109.3333      42.6667       0.0000     152.0000     152.0000
    8     604.8000     179.2000       0.0000     784.0000     784.0000
    9    6044.0889     944.3556     227.5556    7216.0000    7216.0000
   10  107731.6063    7535.9492    1820.4444  117088.0000  117088.0000

  ======================================================================
  THE TOWER OF APPROXIMATIONS
  ======================================================================

  Level 0: P(n) ~ n*T(n)                    [exact for n <= 2]
  Level 1: P(n) ~ n*T(n) - D1(n)            [better approximation]
  Level 2: P(n) ~ n*T(n) - D1(n) - D2(n)    [even better]
  Level 3: P(n) ~ n*T(n) - D1(n) - D2(n) - D3(n)  [exact for n <= ???]

  Each level adds corrections from the next depth of odd partitions.

  Level 0 (P = nT): exact for n <= 2
  Level 1 (P = nT - D1): when does D2 first become nonzero?
    D2 first nonzero at n=6 (layer (3,3))
    So Level 1 is exact for n <= 5
  Level 2 (P = nT - D1 - D2): when does D3 first become nonzero?
    D3 first nonzero at n=9 (layer (3,3,3))
    So Level 2 is exact for n <= 8
  Level 3 (P = nT - D1 - D2 - D3): D4 first at n=12 ((3,3,3,3))
    So Level 3 is exact for n <= 11

  GENERAL: Level d is exact for n <= 3d+2
  (because the (d+1)-th depth requires d+1 three-cycles, needing n >= 3(d+1))

   Level    Exact for  First error at
       0       n <= 2           n = 3
       1       n <= 5           n = 6
       2       n <= 8           n = 9
       3      n <= 11          n = 12

